# Frontend - São Paulo Gas Price Tracker

Frontend implementation for the São Paulo Gas Price Tracker using React and Material-UI.

## Quick Start

```bash
# Install dependencies
npm install

# Set up environment variables
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your Google Maps API key and backend URL

# Start development server
npm start
```

## Structure

```
frontend/
├── src/
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── SearchBar.js      # Location search and radius control
│   │   ├── MapComponent.js   # Google Maps visualization
│   │   └── StationList.js    # Station sidebar
│   ├── context/
│   │   └── StationContext.js # React Context for state management
│   ├── services/
│   │   └── api.js            # Backend API integration
│   ├── config.js             # Application configuration
│   ├── App.js                # Main component
│   └── index.js              # Entry point
├── public/
│   └── index.html            # HTML template
└── package.json              # Dependencies
```

## Features

✅ **Spatial Search** - Find stations within 1-5km radius
✅ **Map Visualization** - Google Maps with color-coded markers
✅ **Station List** - Sorted by price with distance calculation
✅ **Responsive Design** - Desktop and mobile layouts
✅ **Material-UI** - Professional UI components
✅ **React Context** - Centralized state management

## API Integration

- Base URL: `http://localhost:8000` (configurable via .env)
- Uses FastAPI backend endpoints from Phase 2
